    "chunk_size_bytes": 1618,
    "chunk_text": "\u2018Many an educational reform comes to grief because of hasty implementation without adequate preparation. Not only does this defeat the objectives of the reforms but it invariably causes irreparable damage to the younger generation that becomes the guinea pig of such abortive reforms. Therefore, once the reforms have been accepted after public debate and discussion in legislature all necessary safeguards will be taken to ensure that pupils and students, for whose benefit these reforms are being drawn up do not come by any disabilities as a result of poor planning or implementation\u2019 \u201d\n\nHon. Prime Minister, one other thing we need to understand is that the world is changing. AI is taking over most of the current jobs, but it is also creating new jobs. Even teachers themselves may be replaced by technology.\n\nHon. Prime Minister, what are the skills a kid starting Grade 1 in 2026 need for him to do a job when he is 22 years old in 2048? To find that out, what I did was, I asked AI what skills would be required. These are the\n\n1011 1012\n\n\u0dad\u0dca\u0dd4\u0dc0\u0dc4(\u0d86\u0da0\u0daf\u0dca\u0dad )\u0dc4 \u0dca\u0dad\u0dc2\u0dc4:\u0dc4\u0dd2\u0d82\u0dca \u0dc0\u0daf\u0dc4\u0dc4\u0db8\u0dc3 \u0dcf\u0daf\n\n2025 \u0da2\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0dc424\n\nskills: Adaptability and Continuous Learning; the ability to quickly learn new technologies and adapt to changing roles will be paramount; Technology Proficiency; Complex Problem Solving; Communications and Collaboration; Leadership and Social Influence; Creativity and Innovation and Emotional Intelligence. So, those are the skills that they need to have as adults going out to face the global competitive economy. So, the curricula need to change."
