    "chunk_size_bytes": 2008,
    "chunk_text": "1. Inflation has deviated from the inflation target primarily due to pronounced supply-side deflation. As outlined in the published target breach reports, significant reductions in administered prices and costs - especially in electricity and fuel - have really exerted a strong downward pressure on inflation in recent times. In addition, the deflation\n\n1127 1128\n\n2025 \u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dd2 2\n\nAt the same time, it is noteworthy to understand that exceptionally high inflation levels prevailed in the country, especially in 2022 and 2023. Therefore, a brief period of inflation lower than the targeted inflation could, in a way, provide some relief to households and businesses.\n\n2. No. The Central Bank Act was enacted with effect from September, 2023, allowing greater independence to the Central Bank. Accordingly, the Central Bank is not subject to fiscal dominance or any other external constraints.\n\n3. The enactment of the Act is a major structural reform and according to Section 8, the Act establishes a Governing Board to oversee the tasks and the general policy decisions other than monetary policy and enforcement measures. Further, according to Section 11 of the Act, the Monetary Policy Board has been established to deal with a flexible exchange rate regime in line with flexible inflation targeting framework to achieve and maintain domestic price stability.\n\nIn support of policy transparency and accountability, the Act mandates the Central Bank to publish the Monetary Policy Framework Agreement between the Ministry of Finance and the Central Bank, outlining inflation targets according to Section 26. It also defines the requirement of the Central Bank to submit reports to Parliament and make them available to the general public, if the inflation target specified in the Monetary Policy Framework Agreement is not met. So, that has been done. In addition, every six months, another report on inflation is published. The third report, which is on the state of economy, is also submitted annually."
