    "md5": "179447d7ebe34ecac2ebd7df6fb53d26",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1945,
    "chunk_text": "In support of policy transparency and accountability, the Act mandates the Central Bank to publish the Monetary Policy Framework Agreement between the Ministry of Finance and the Central Bank, outlining inflation targets according to Section 26. It also defines the requirement of the Central Bank to submit reports to Parliament and make them available to the general public, if the inflation target specified in the Monetary Policy Framework Agreement is not met. So, that has been done. In addition, every six months, another report on inflation is published. The third report, which is on the state of economy, is also submitted annually.\n\n4. Under the framework of Flexible Inflation Targeting - FIT - the Central Bank has taken appropriate and prudent monetary policy measures proactively, while maintaining a flexible exchange rate policy, as stipulated by the Act.\n\n5. The Monetary Policy Board carries out its independent assessment and reviews inflation performance under the IMF Extended Fund Facility programme, which is being monitored by the IMF staff and reviewed by the IMF Executive Board. These assessments are in the public domain and are available on the IMF website as well.\n\n6. Yes. There are specific requirements prescribed in the Act in the event of deviations from the targets and since, consecutively, two quarters were\n\nmissed, the Central Bank has submitted the necessary information to Parliament. Those procedures and provisions are prescribed in the amended Act.\n\nThe Inflation Target Agreement was signed in 2023. It is valid for three years and will end in 2026. The target set was 5 per cent. That had been determined based on the facts, figures and research done, again within the band of 2 per cent upside and downside, which means that it could vary from 3 per cent to 7 per cent. However, the downward slab - the 3 per cent - is not that much of a worry since it does not really hike the inflation further."
