    "chunk_text": "The Inflation Target Agreement was signed in 2023. It is valid for three years and will end in 2026. The target set was 5 per cent. That had been determined based on the facts, figures and research done, again within the band of 2 per cent upside and downside, which means that it could vary from 3 per cent to 7 per cent. However, the downward slab - the 3 per cent - is not that much of a worry since it does not really hike the inflation further.\n\n8. As per the Central Bank\u2019s review, it is not applicable because the Bank does not attribute the deviation of inflation from the target to fiscal activities.\n\n9. The Act endorses the Monetary Policy Framework Agreement with regard to setting out the inflation target to be achieved by the Central Bank. Accordingly, this framework was signed between the Hon. Minister of Finance and the Governor of the Central Bank on 03rd October, 2023."
