    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "d24e3947f2679e70d2e034187c23acc1",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1007,
    "chunk_text": "A principled politician who unwaveringly championed social justice, he earned deep respect, both locally and internationally. He consistently advocated for peace and the rights of the Sri Lankan people, often representing their cause on numerous official visits abroad.\n\nHe was married to Mrs. Leeladevi and was a loving father of two sons and a daughter.\n\nSir, several times, we have been trying our best to take up the Vote of Condolence on the death of the Hon. Sampanthan, but due to some issues we were not able to do that. We can see the family members of the Hon. Sampanthan participating on this occasion and we welcome them on behalf of Parliament.\n\nSir, death of a mature politician like the Hon. Sampanthan is an unfillable void on the political sphere of Sri Lanka. We pray that the late Hon. Rajavarothiam Sampanthan attain the state he aspired to in accordance with his religious belief, and request that this august Assembly convey its condolences to his beloved wife, children and relatives."
