    "chunk_size_bytes": 1979,
    "chunk_text": "He first entered Parliament by winning the March, 1960 Parliamentary Elections, representing the Kalawana Constituency and throughout his political career, the Hon. Pilapitiya contested the Kalawana Seat five times as a candidate of the United National Party at the Parliamentary Elections held in March, 1960, July, 1960, 1965, 1970 and 1977. Notably, he emerged victorious in three of those contests, specifically at the Elections held in March, 1960, 1965 and 1977. His dedication and leadership qualities led him to the position of Deputy Minister of Posts and Telecommunication, a role he executed with distinction.\n\nFinally, Sir, I would like to speak about the late Hon. Rajavarothiam Sampanthan, who was the Leader of the Tamil National Alliance and also our party. He was also a Leader of the Opposition. So, I have to say a few words on behalf of him.\n\nThe late Hon. Sampanthan served this House for over half a century across multiple chapters of Sri Lanka\u2019s post-Independence history. His Parliamentary career was not just long, but was principled. It was shaped by an unwavering commitment to justice, democracy and most of all, the dignity and the political rights of the Tamil people. He believed in meaningful power-sharing, reconciliation without erasure, accountability and in a just and an honourable solution to the national question. He sought peace, not surrender. He spoke gently, but the truth he carried thundered through the halls and beyond this Parliament. What set the Hon. Sampanthan apart was not just his intellect or experience, but his moral clarity. He refused to abandon our cause even when it was politically inconvenient or personally costly and through it all, he conducted himself with a grace that earned the respect of both the allies and adversaries. He believed in dialogue, but never at the cost of principle. He carried forward the mandate of a wounded and often silenced community and carried it with immense grace and discipline."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
