    "chunk_size_bytes": 2178,
    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dc0 \u0d9a\u0d9c\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf[\u0d9a\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dd2, \u0dc1\u0db8\u0dca \u0dc3\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0db1\u0dca\u0db0\u0dc1[\u0db1\u0dca \u0d9c\u0dad\u0dca\u0dc1\u0dad\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dca, \u0dc3\u0dcf\u0dd4\u0dba \u0dc11\u0da0\u0dcf1\u0da7 \u0db1\u0dd41\u0dba \u0d92\u0dc1\u0d9c\u0dcf\u0dca \u0da0\u0db1\u0dca \u0dc1\u0d9c\u0db1\u0dca\u0db1\u0dca \u0dad\u0daf\u0da0\u0dcf \u0d91\u0dc5\u0dd2[\u0da7 \u0daf\u0dcf\u0db1 \u0dad\u0dad\u0dca\u0dad\u0dca1[\u0d9a \u0dad\u0dad\u0dd2 \u0dc11\u0da0\u0dcf \u0dad\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0db6\u0db11\u0dcf. \u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca \u0d91\u0d9a \u0d91\u0dc5\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0dad [\u0db1 \u0d9c\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dca \u0d85\u0dba\u0dc1\u0d9c\u0db1 [\u0db1 \u0d851\u0dc3\u0dda\u0d9c\u0dcf \u0dad\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0db6\u0db11\u0dcf. \u0d89\u0dad\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dca, \u0dcf\u0dcf \u0dc1\u0db8\u0dca \u0dcf\u0db1\u0dd4\u0dc2\u0dca\u0da8\u0dba\u0db7\u0dcf1\u0dc1[\u0db1\u0dca \u0dad\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dca \u0dc1\u0db8\u0dca \u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dba\u0dab[ \u0d85\u0dd4\u0db1\u0dca\u0dc1\u0db1\u0dca.\n\n1497 1498\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0db8\u0dca\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db81\n\nAccordingly, I seek urgent responses and policy clarity on the following key questions:\n\n\uf0b7 Can the Central Bank provide data on how many asset seizures occur annually, and how many involve individuals facing economic hardship rather than willful non-payment?\n\n2. Why does the Central Bank permit the seizure of mortgaged assets such as vehicles after just 90 to 120 days of non-payment, without mandating any assessment of the lessee\u2019s financial hardship, intent or willingness to negotiate?\n\n3. Can the Central Bank introduce or recommend guidelines to financial institutions to differentiate between willful defaulters and genuine hardship cases and mandate negotiated settlements or restructuring options before seizure proceedings are initiated?\n\n4. Has the Central Bank considered introducing a mandatory \u201cGrace period mechanism\u201d or a mediation board to be consulted prior to the seizure of leased property \u2013 especially for micro and small enterprise operators who rely on such assets for income generation?\n\n5. What are the legal remedies currently available to lessees who allege unfair repossession of their leased assets? Has the Central Bank ever intervened in cases where financial institutions were found to have acted with undue haste or without exploring restructuring options?\n\n6. Will the Central Bank commit to a policy review of the leasing sector, particularly to examine the impact of harsh seizure practices on small business owners, self-employed individuals and low-income earners so that a more equitable and humane framework could be instituted?"
