 proposed CSA deviates from the merits and principles of the Bill and therefore is inconsistent with Article 78(3) of the Constitution.\u201d\n\nBut, I say that the Attorney-General\u2019s representative does not explain how or why moving LTL Holdings Limited from the NTNSP to a residual company conflicts with Article 78(3) of the Constitution. So, I would like to ask the Attorney-General himself to explain to this House how that Committee Stage Amendment on moving LTL Holdings Limited deviates from the merits and principles of this Bill because it is a critical matter. \u0d92 \u0dd2\u0db4\u0dd2[ \u0dcf\u0dcf \u0dc1\u0db8\u0dca \u0d851\u0dc3\u0dda\u0d9c\u0dcf\u0dc1\u0dda\u0daf\u0dd3 \u0dc3\u0dca\u0db7\u0dcf \u0dad* \u0d9a\u0dba\u0db11\u0dcf."
