    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "712849222f0276eb741d276080758cd4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1112,
    "chunk_text": "Then, I will move on to some other issue which is now being discussed in the energy circles. That is regarding the 2025 tariff revision for Standard Power Purchasing Agreements governing projects up to 10 megawatts. Though this revision is presented as a routine, cost-reflective recalibration cloaked with references to the International Monetary Fund and its conditionality, the substance reveals a different story. This is not a correction; this is sabotage, a systemic, deliberate distortion by a group with vested interests that threatens to derail the Government\u2019s own renewable energy goals.\n\n1575 1576\n\n\u0dd3\u0d9c\u0dc0 \u0dc0 1\u0db1\u0dca \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0dda\u0dd3\u0dba \u0dcf\u0dd4\u0dad\u0dcf\n\n2025 \u0d85\u0dc1\u0d9c\u0ddd\u0dc3\u0dda\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8 6\n\nare allowed US Dollar-pegged tariffs, protecting larger, often foreign-backed projects from foreign exchange risk. Why is this inconsistency? Are we creating a tariff regime that rewards size, not merit? Are we discouraging distributed, citizen-led renewable investments while paving the way for large, centralized fossil fuel infrastructure? This is not just poor design, but also structural discrimination."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2025-08-06-2025-08-06",
    "num": "2025-08-06",
    "date_str": "2025-08-06",
    "description": "Hansard of August 06, 2025",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/documents/hansard/1755159820030645.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2025-08-06-2025-08-06-0159",
    "chunk_index": 159,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "2a4fa36c103a276204d4bba61053e3d8",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2501,
    "chunk_text": "are allowed US Dollar-pegged tariffs, protecting larger, often foreign-backed projects from foreign exchange risk. Why is this inconsistency? Are we creating a tariff regime that rewards size, not merit? Are we discouraging distributed, citizen-led renewable investments while paving the way for large, centralized fossil fuel infrastructure? This is not just poor design, but also structural discrimination.\n\n\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0dc3\u0dca\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd6\u0daa \u0db8\u0dcf\u0dad\u0db1\u0dca\u0dd3\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0ba4\u0bae\u0bb2\u0bae\u0bc8\u0ba4\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b89\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Presiding Member) \u0d9c\u0dc0 \u0dcf\u0db1\u0dca\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf\u0dcf, \u0d94\u0db6\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf\u0dcf\u0da7 \u0db1\u0dd2[\u0dd2\u0dba\u0dad \u0d9a\u0dcf\u0da0[ \u0d851\u0dc3\u0dcf\u0db1\u0db1\u0dca. \u0d9a\u0dc0 \u0dab\u0dcf\u0d9a\u0dba \u0d9a\u0d9c\u0dcf1 \u0d851\u0dc3\u0db1\u0dca \u0d9a\u0dba\u0db1\u0dca\u0db1.\n\n\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd2\u0da5 \u0dbb\u0dc0\u0dd4\u0dc6\u0dad \u0dc4\u0d9a\u0dd3\u0db8\u0dca \u0db8\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bb0\u0ba3\u0bbf \u0bb0\u0b8a\u0baa\u0bcd \u0bb9\u0b95\u0bc0\u0bae\u0bcd) (The Hon. Rauff Hakeem, Attorney-at-Law) Parliament should request the subject Minister and the Hon. President to appoint a high-powered committee consisting of non-conflicted professionals who are not aligned to the power industry to deep dive and unravel the maze of entities with cross shareholding and also figure out the net worth of shareholdings of former public servants in this LTL venture. Sir, it is said that there are employees' trust companies which have been formed and are hidden. \u0dc1\u0db8\u0dca \u0dc1\u0d9a\u0dcf\u0da7\u0dc3\u0dda 1\u0dba\u0d82\u0d9c\u0dc1[\u0db1\u0dca, 1\u200d\u0dbb\u0dcf\u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dba\u0dc1[\u0db1\u0dca \u0db4\u0dcf\u0da0\u0db1[ \u0d9a\u0dba\u0db1 \u0db4\u0dd0\u0db1\u0dd0\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd2[\u0d9a \u0dc1\u0dcf[ \u0d85\u0dc3\u0dda\u0dc1\u0dc3\u0dda \u0d89\u0db1\u0dca\u0db11\u0dcf\u0daf \u0dd2\u0dbb[\u0db1 \u0d91\u0d9a \u0db4\u0dd2\u0dc5\u0dd2\u0db6\u0db31 \u0d85\u0db4\u0da7 \u0dc0\u0dd2 \u0dcf\u0da0 \u0dca\u200d\u0dbb \u0dda\u0db1[\u0d9a \u0dad\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0db6\u0db11\u0dcf. \u0dc1\u0db8\u0dca \u0db4\u0dd2\u0dc5\u0dd2\u0db6\u0db31 \u0dc1\u0dc3\u0dcf[\u0dcf \u0db6\u0dd0\u0dd2[ \u0dba\u0dd4\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0db1\u0dca; \u0dc1\u0db8\u0dca\u0dc1\u0d9a \u0dad\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0db6\u0db1 1\u0d82\u0db1\u0dcf1 \u0dc1\u0dd4\u0dc5\u0dd2\u0daf\u0dba\u0dda \u0d9a\u0db1 \u0dba\u0dd4\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0db1\u0dca. Sir, we saw that there was an IPO worth almost Rs. 20 billion. This entity is worth more than Rs. 100 billion today. So, how can there be such a large amount of shareholding of a few public servants, who had been attached to the Ceylon Electricity Board, in charge of the LTL and are now controlling this mafia? Therefore, that has to be looked into. I call upon the Government to look into it very seriously; particularly, the Chairman of the LTL should now initiate an inquiry and let the public know what is happening inside that institution.\n\nThank you."
  },
