    "md5": "fceba3ec2e2db7b512739117f7b0bdf3",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2266,
    "chunk_text": "Sir, one main question asked by the Opposition and the public is, will this restructuring reduce the tariff? The short answer is, yes, but with a realistic and phased approach. So, immediate cost reductions will come from introducing competition in power procurement, phasing out costly emergency power purchases, reducing technical and commercial losses and leveraging digital efficiencies. The other question asked is whether there will be an issue for the current workforce. This reform is not for dismantling of the workforce, but for transformation of the institution. The proposed Amendments include a 100 per cent government-owned employees' fund to secure pensions and welfare. Then, there will be employment guarantee for the employees in this transition to the new institutions under this new restructuring or the excess employees could go on voluntarily retirement through a VRS, safeguarding the current staff and their rights. Also, this restructuring involves training and upskilling of the current CEB employees to take on the future-ready roles. Then, transparent communication and HR restructuring to prevent uncertainty and fear are also included in the plan.\n\nLet us rise above short-term political goals and act in the long-term national interest. Let us make electricity efficient, affordable, transparent and digital, as in any modern economy. I urge this House to pass these Amendments not for political credit, but for the benefit of the people we have been elected to serve.\n\nI thank you, Sir, for giving me the opportunity to speak in this Debate.\n\n\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0dc3\u0dca\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd6\u0daa \u0db8\u0dcf\u0dad\u0db1\u0dca\u0dd3\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0ba4\u0bae\u0bb2\u0bae\u0bc8\u0ba4\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b89\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Presiding Member) \u0d9c\u0dc0 \u0d91\u0db8\u0dca.\u0d92.\u0d91\u0db8\u0dca. \u0dad\u0dcf\u0dc4\u0dd2\u0dbb\u0dca \u0dcf\u0db1\u0dca\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf\u0dcf. \u0d94\u0db6\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf\u0dcf\u0da7 \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dcf\u0da9\u0dd2 0\u0d9a \u0d9a\u0dcf\u0da0[\u0d9a \u0dad\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0db6\u0db11\u0dcf.\n\n[\u0baa\u0bbf.\u0baa. 4.14]\n\n\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d91\u0db8\u0dca.\u0d92.\u0d91\u0db8\u0dca. \u0dad\u0dcf\u0dd2\u0dc0\u0dbb\u0dca \u0db8\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b8e\u0bae\u0bcd.\u0b8f.\u0b8e\u0bae\u0bcd. \u0ba4\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0bb9\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0bcd) (The Hon. M.A.M. Thahir) \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb8\u0bcd\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd\u0bb2\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0bb9\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0bb0\u0bb9\u0bcd\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba9\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0bb0\u0bb9\u0bc0\u0bae\u0bcd."
