    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "121ecba0128fcdeed84985c36e9385ee",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1820,
    "chunk_text": "Another thing that we need to understand is that though we have moved from crisis to stability, in achieving economic growth, the IMF programme is restrictive in certain ways on Government expenditure. So, with that, we are trying to prioritize our expenditure to support our industries. We are also trying to support the marginalized communities, ensuring that we are within the growth trajectory, which we see from the data that was produced today.\n\nThe next issue is, misinformation about foreign direct investments. We have enough foreign direct investments coming in. We had Inquiries for investments for over US Dollars 4.6 billion and we have already secured US Dollars 536 million of foreign direct investments, which is a growth of about 100 per cent compared to last year. Also, under the Ministry of Industries, we have given approval to start 78 factories, which will be started during this year and in the first half of next year.\n\n1767 1768\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dae\u0dd2\u0dba\u0db8\u0dca\u0db1\u0dca\u0dc0\u0dc0\n\nSo, I am going to wind up saying that the country is moving forward, taking the economy from stability to growth and here, the request for the Opposition is to be part of this journey because Sri Lanka is transforming. Sri Lanka is transforming with reforms to the legal structure, changing the bad political culture and the Government going after the people who wasted public money.\n\n\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd2\u0d9c\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bcd \u0b9a\u0baa\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Deputy Speaker) Hon. Chathurange Abeysinghe, your time is up. \u0dd4 \u0da0\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0d82 \u0d85\u0d9c\u0dc3\u0dc3\u0dd2\u0d82\u0dc4\u0dc3 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u