    "md5": "ec20a9d8858e06b56df1b55d283cdc79",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2009,
    "chunk_text": "The other is, at our borders, the practical regime permits any amount to be brought or taken with declarations required at US Dollars 15,000 of total foreign exchange and US Dollars 10,000 in currency notes. Declarations alone are not a control on downstream use. Without a bank-rail mandate inside casinos, this becomes the perfect pretext for cash-based foreign exchange recycling, rent-seeking and corruption risks in the cage.\n\nSir, what is the core inconsistency here? We should promote gambling tourism as a current account service consistent with Article VIII of the IMF Agreement. But, \"promoting\" cannot mean pay in and cash out in foreign\n\nexchange notes at a front desk. Promotion in a current account-convertible economy must mean frictionless, bank-channel settlement with strong AML/CFT safeguards. Today\u2019s Bill locks in the opposite. Therefore, I have a detailed suggestion and I table* it so that that could be taken into account.\n\nSir, we are a current account-convertible country. That means, we facilitate legitimate current transactions including gambling services, but through banks and regulated PSPs with real-time reporting and tight oversight. Our peers show that it is possible. There are Singapore\u2019s thresholds and data-sharing, UK\u2019s CDD rule and crime prevention mandate and also similar things in Macau and other places. Also, there is a clampdown on junkets and joint liability in Macau. Let us import those guardrails, rather than importing past mistakes. That is what we are saying. This Bill, as drafted, creates a cash-first front desk, ignores banking channel settlement and leaves junkets unregulated, which are going to create serious problems in the future. This will create a haven for various other people.\n\nIn the meantime, what do the very people who have come here and set up those businesses now say? This particular Melco Resorts, who have come here and set up a casino business with the John Keells Holdings, states this in its Annual Report, 2024, I quote:"
  },
