    "chunk_text": "Therefore, with time running out and risks mounting, this House and the people deserve clear and measurable answers on how the Government intends to transform our export performances, diversify markets, conclude meaningful trade agreements, attract new investments and to protect exporters from adverse global trade policies.\n\nAccordingly, I wish to ask the Hon. Minister of Finance, Planning and Economic Development the following:\n\nHon. Deputy Minister, as you know, that 20 per cent is added on to another 10 per cent and 13 per cent. So, altogether, there would be a 38.4 per cent tax on Sri Lanka with regard to trade is what has been mentioned.\n\n4. Market diversification and trade agreements: How many new trade agreements or preferential access arrangements would be finalized by 2030? Why are previously signed agreements not operational yet and what new countries or regions are being targeted? Is Sri Lanka considering joining any regional trade groupings?\n\nHon. Speaker, the Free Trade Agreements with Singapore and Thailand had been signed, sealed and delivered, but are not put into operation. What particular problem is causing delay?"
