    "chunk_size_bytes": 2003,
    "chunk_text": "\u0dd4 \u0dbb\u0dd3 \u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dab\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a \u0dd9\u0dad\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bb0\u0bb5\u0bbf \u0b95\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95) (The Hon. Ravi Karunanayake) Hon. Speaker, an article published in the \u201cDaily Mirror\u201d newspaper of August 13, 2025 states that more than 50 per cent of students graduating from State universities in several standard subject areas leave the country and never return. It also states that that has been revealed by a research conducted by Professors Wasantha Athukorala and Lakshman Kumara of the University of Peradeniya.\n\nEvery student who graduates from our universities gets that opportunity because the rupees of the common people such as farmers, workers, teachers and small business owners have been invested. However, a strange and worrying trend that we see increasingly is that immediately after graduating, people go abroad without fulfilling their legal and contractual obligation of serving the country for even a minimum period of time. That is not only a waste of money, but also a waste of human and financial resources. That is a drain of our capacity, causes a slowdown in national development and even a defeat for the very purpose of providing free education. When graduates violate their contracts and go abroad without rendering any service to the country, they destroy the trust of the country and deprive the generations to come of the same opportunities.\n\nAfter the Government, the taxpayers and the public invest in education of a doctor, engineer, accountant or a scientist, if they leave without serving the country for even a short period of time, it could be considered a public investment made for another country.\n\nSo, will the Sri Lankan people continue to spend funds on education of those who have no intention of actually serving the country? Or should we not make it mandatory for those who violate the contract to repay the full cost of their education, whether legally or otherwise, if they do not serve the country for a period of time?"
  },
