    "chunk_text": "\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dda\u0dcf\u0dca \u0b95\u0bc1\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0b95\u0b95 \u0ba8\u0bbf\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0bb5\u0ba9\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0ba4\u0b95\u0bbe\u0bb3\u0bcd\u0b95\u0b95\u0b95\u0b95\u0bb3\n\n\u0bae\u0bc0\u0bb3\u0bbe\u0baf\u0bcd\u0bb5\u0bc1 \u0ba4\u0b9a\u0baf\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bb2\u0bcd: \u0ba4\u0ba4\u0bbe\u0bb4\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0b85\u0b95\u0bae\u0b9a\u0bcd\u0b9a\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd\n\n\u0ba4\u0baa\u0bbe\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0bb3\u0bbe\u0ba4\u0bbe\u0bb0 \u0b85\u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb5\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0baa\u0bcd \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\n\n\u0b85\u0b95\u0bae\u0b9a\u0bcd\u0b9a\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba9\u0bb5\u0bbe\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0ba4\u0bc1 \u0b95\u0bc2\u0bb1\u0bcd\u0bb1\u0bc1 REVIEWAL OF POLICIES IN LEASING SECTOR:\n\nSTATEMENT BY MINISTER OF LABOUR AND\n\nDEPUTY MINISTER OF ECONOMIC\n\n1. Question No. 1 pertains to lease contracts and the Central Bank\u2019s involvement in it. The Central Bank of Sri Lanka has not issued specific or separate regulatory directions to provide protection for all the borrowers who face involuntary default in the leasing sector. The existing Financial Consumer Protection Framework and Regulations are applicable to all the borrowers appropriately.\n\nDirection on Customer Charter of Licensed Banks\n\nand direction on Financial Customer Protection Framework for Finance Companies and Specialized Leasing Companies were issued in 2011 and 2018, respectively with the objective of safeguarding the interests of customers, maintaining a healthy relationship with them and strengthening customer confidence.\n\nFurther, the Financial Consumer Protection Regulation issued on 09.08.2023 states that financial service providers, including their agents or third parties acting on their behalf, must not engage in unfair business practices that harm financial consumers. It also states that financial service providers must not act in bad faith or display negligence when offering financial products or services. The term \u201cunfair business practices\u201d includes deceptive, abusive or misleading conduct, aggressive debt collection methods, increasing credit limits without obtaining prior consent from the consumer and imposing excessive fees, penalties, future interest or charges that are disproportionate to the actual cost incurred et cetera.\n\n2409 2410\n\n[\u0db1\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d85 \u0dc4\u0dca\u0dab \u0dcf\u0dca\u200d\u0d9c\u0dda \u0d85\u0dbd\u0da9\u0d9a\u0dca\u0d9a\u0dba\u0dda\u0dbd \u0d8b \u0dcf\u0dca\u200d\u0d9c\u0dda \u0db8 \u0dab\u0dcf]\n\n2025 \u0d85 \u0db1 \u0dc3\u0dca\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dc0\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8 22\n\nFurther, the recovery actions are mainly governed by the terms and conditions agreed to between licensed banks, finance companies or specialized leasing companies and borrowers through finance leasing and loan agreements."
