    "chunk_size_bytes": 1129,
    "chunk_text": "5. Borrowers are able to seek redress through the Mediation Boards or the Financial Ombudsman. Further, a customer who is subject to unfair treatment can lodge a complaint to the Financial Consumer Relations Department of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka. The Central Bank of Sri Lanka may call for additional information/documents, for a hearing from all/any party involved and/or conduct a spot examination/inquiry, as applicable. Based on the determination, the Central Bank of Sri Lanka may require LBs/FCs/SLCs to take specific actions where necessary. Also, borrowers have the option to take necessary legal action under contract or consumer law.\n\n07. At present, the Central Bank of Sri Lanka collects information from three banks - licensed banks,\n\nfinance companies and specialized leasing companies - for supervisory purposes. Therefore, the granular level breakdown of leasing contracts is not available with the Central Bank of Sri Lanka. The large institutions have a large market share due to their wider branch networks, availability of resources et cetera and not necessarily due to regulatory asymmetry.\n\nThank you."
  },
