    "chunk_text": "However, if we look around what is happening globally, from what we are witnessing today, there are important lessons for us to learn as a new Government: the importance of strong and committed leadership and having strong institutions which could withstand the pressures of change and corruption and most importantly, the importance of inculcating a culture of respect for human rights in any society. We can see how easily institutions could be dismantled or weakened, if that culture of respect for human rights is not normalized or accepted within a society.\n\n2479 2480\n\n\u0db0\u0dcf\u0dca\u0db8\u0dd2 \u0db8\u0dca\u0d9c\u0dda\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dc0\n\nthere for over 70 years in this country; this is what we inherited. These institutions, these norms, these laws, this general sense of who we are, all of this is what we are dealing with today and what we must address and, in many instances, dismantle. We cannot dismiss lightly the impact of the political culture that had been maintained and survived in this country during those years till not barely a year ago and what it had meant for us as a people and as a country.\n\nMadam, it is also correct to say that if we look at all the perpetrators who have participated in violations of human rights, even those at the lowest level, many may not have intended to be evil; they might not even have considered themselves evil, wicked or even as breaking the law.\n\nBut, it was this culture of impunity, abuse and racism which allowed them to do what they did and not feel as if they had committed an act of unspeakable evil. So, that is the reality we have to confront and dismantle in this country.\n\nAgain, may I refer to another Italian philosopher, Hannah Arendt, who had written widely on these issues and this is something she had said, I quote:\n\n\u201cThe sad truth is that most evil is done by people who never make up their minds to be good or evil.\u201d"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2025-08-22-2025-08-22",
    "num": "2025-08-22",
    "date_str": "2025-08-22",
    "description": "Hansard of August 22, 2025",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/documents/hansard/1756894696039492.pdf",
