    "chunk_size_bytes": 1996,
    "chunk_text": "[2.44 p.m.] \u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd2\u0db4\u0da5 \u0dbb\u0dc0\u0dd4\u0dc6\u0dad \u0dad\u0d9a\u0dd3\u0db8\u0dca \u0dd9\u0dad\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bb0\u0bc8\u0bbf \u0bb0\u0b8a\u0baa\u0bcd \u0bb9\u0b95\u0bc0\u0bae\u0bcd) (The Hon. Rauff Hakeem, Attorney-at-Law) Hon. Deputy Chairperson of Committees, I am glad to follow our affable Prime Minister, the Hon. (Dr.) Harini Amarasuriya. She, in her inimitable style, delivered a very sensible speech, perhaps, regarding the Adjournment Motion that has been moved today. She, in her own style, referred to those pending issues with the sensitivities involved in them and said that they are very keen to bring the culture of impunity to an end to create a new sensible culture, a new era, which is to unfold from now onwards with the new regime in power.\n\n2483 2484\n\n\u0db0\u0dcf\u0dca\u0db8\u0dd2 \u0db8\u0dca\u0d9c\u0dda\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dc0\n\nformer Heads of State to be treated in this manner. The Hon. Minister of Justice and National Integration is a very senior criminal practitioner and he knows that that is the normal practice. Everybody should be treated equally, but when it comes to a former President, at least, some courtesies, minimum courtesies should be extended to him. That is my humble opinion and I do not want to say anything beyond regarding that matter.\n\nHaving said that, let me also speak about another matter since the Hon. Minister of Foreign Affairs is in the Chamber now. There is this particular Report by the Office of the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights. That is to be debated from 08th of September onwards for one whole month. That is going to take place in Geneva and I am sure the Government is getting ready to meet all the challenges that would be made in Geneva. But, what pertains here is some reference made to the Attorney-General\u2019s Department. This Government has gone on record saying that they will create a new Public Prosecutor's Office. That is a welcome move. But, let us take into account what the UN High Commissioner for Human Rights says in his Report. I quote:"
  },
