    "md5": "25577c304782acc6b85d001f62996b0a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1539,
    "chunk_text": "The Minister of Foreign Affairs, my Minister, made a historic speech today. He also emphasized the need to repeal the PTA and especially mentioned that by early September, a repeal Bill would be presented to Parliament, which, we feel, would be one of the major turning points. I, as a Member of the JVP, know that the PTA was brought in during the 70s\u2019 and our party was one of the key victims of the PTA. If that was brought in for oppression, we believe that, now, we have the chance to repeal that and replace it with something which is not oppressive. But, if we need to address certain issues like underworld activities or some drug-related crimes, we would introduced some legislation on par with the global judicial system, but that would not be an oppressive law.\n\nAlso, we have to address certain issues related to land in this country. Sir, as you know, this country was experiencing a different political culture for the last 76 plus years and now, we have the chance and a mandate to change certain things. If we take land-related matters which involve the Department of Forest Conservation, the Department of Wildlife Conservation, the Department of Archaeology, the defence authorities and various other\n\nbodies, certain people's lands had been taken over by them during the war time. And, certain lands were being used by them for cultivation purposes. So, for certain reasons, those lands were taken over. All the Governments that were in power before the NPP came to power were not interested in solving those problems."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2025-08-22-2025-08-22",
    "num": "2025-08-22",
    "date_str": "2025-08-22",
    "description": "Hansard of August 22, 2025",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
