    "chunk_text": "Sir, let me now move on to certain specific information and facts on how the security forces are being informed, educated and be made aware of the value of human rights and how best they should protected. Also, we believe that the rule of law is the foundation principle of democratic governance and the cornerstone of national security. It also provides the framework for protecting civil liberties, ensuring Government's accountability and maintaining public trust in institutions.\n\nThen, out of a total of 85,486 acres of State and private lands in the North and the East held and used by the military over a period of time, since 2009, we have released over 75,000 acres up to 21st of August and I will table* these statistics for the record.\n\nMore lands are to be released in the years to come. Next year, another 12,000 acres are planned to be released. About another 12,738 acres are still being held by the military, taking into consideration the strategic values, security concerns and the camps that have to be there to ensure national security. Then, the lands scheduled to be released this year include another 700 acres of State land and 43 acres of private land. Those lands will also be released very soon.\n\nIn Jaffna, we have opened the road running from Vasavilan Junction to the T-junction, which had been closed for over three decades. The Pulmoddai-Kokkilai"
