    "description": "Hansard of September 09, 2025",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/documents/hansard/1757672711095734.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2025-09-09-2025-09-09-0250",
    "chunk_index": 250,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "7c2c066e7e8e450bec5595c92389f14e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1759,
    "chunk_text": "But, Sir, there is a much more urgent matter brewing in the Middle East and even the United Arab Emirates has already pointed out that if Israel continues to go ahead with their plan to occupy the land of the Palestinians, they would cross the red-line and would damage the spirit of the Abraham Accords, which normalized the relationship between the two countries.\n\nSir, the demographics of Gaza, the West Bank and East Jerusalem, the three key Occupied Territories that were on the Middle East map before 07th October, 2023, have fast been altered for nearly two years to date. It is brutally evident that new facts are being created on the ground through a deadly combination of political, military, ideology-based strategies which have snuffed out the innocent lives of more than 60,000 people and displaced over 2 million people, half of them children. The aggressors have now begun to target Palestinian people in the other areas of the Occupied Territory as well. No decent, democratic, conscientious nation or people could be reticent or worse, collusive over these violent catastrophes, which the world witnesses with shattered hearts day in and day out.\n\nThe fundamental premise that should have ideally underpinned a reasonably negotiated political settlement to the Palestinian question since 1948, the Nakba, which means forced displacement and dispossession of the Palestinians, have now been turned on their head. The right of the refugees of the Nakba era and their descendants to return to Palestine has effectively been throttled. Under international law, it is a right that should be fostered and facilitated. Rather, the reality today is far more ominous with more and more Palestinians risk expulsion or evacuation from their territories."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2025-09-09-2025-09-09",
