    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/documents/hansard/1757672711095734.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2025-09-09-2025-09-09-0251",
    "chunk_index": 251,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "dde801b2cfd2a99c85aac7e64e63a4b5",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1809,
    "chunk_text": "The fundamental premise that should have ideally underpinned a reasonably negotiated political settlement to the Palestinian question since 1948, the Nakba, which means forced displacement and dispossession of the Palestinians, have now been turned on their head. The right of the refugees of the Nakba era and their descendants to return to Palestine has effectively been throttled. Under international law, it is a right that should be fostered and facilitated. Rather, the reality today is far more ominous with more and more Palestinians risk expulsion or evacuation from their territories.\n\nSri Lanka recognized the State of Palestine as far back as 1989. Consequently, the Palestinian diplomatic representation in Colombo had been recognized as the\n\n123 124\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dca\u0daf \u0da2\u0dba\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dc4 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n2025 \u0dc3\u0dd0\u0db4\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd0\u0dda\u0dd9\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd 2\n\nEmbassy of the State of Palestine in terms of the Vienna Convention on Diplomatic Relations. It is our national responsibility to assert that recognition on every platform, regional and international as well as bilateral and multilateral. Not doing it as assiduously as such State recognition entails or behaving in a manner that chips away at the core of that recognition means that the Government does not care whether that State so recognized exists or goes off the face of the earth.\n\nIt is not just a treachery committed against the Palestinian people, but also an imprimatur of approval for the ongoing anti-Palestine abolitionist project, which, if successful, would undoubtedly have wider ramifications on regional security and stability, including on Sri Lanka. We, as Representatives of people, should ensure that the Palestinian people are not denied their due place and all attempts to reduce them to subhumans are frustrated."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2025-09-09-2025-09-09",
    "num": "2025-09-09",
    "date_str": "2025-09-09",
    "description": "Hansard of September 09, 2025",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/documents/hansard/1757672711095734.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2025-09-09-2025-09-09-0252",
    "chunk_index": 252,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "9430158d09b6e36e1f129f680dd93cee",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1720,
    "chunk_text": "It is not just a treachery committed against the Palestinian people, but also an imprimatur of approval for the ongoing anti-Palestine abolitionist project, which, if successful, would undoubtedly have wider ramifications on regional security and stability, including on Sri Lanka. We, as Representatives of people, should ensure that the Palestinian people are not denied their due place and all attempts to reduce them to subhumans are frustrated.\n\nSir, it is high time that the Government of Sri Lanka call a spade a spade and directly and unequivocally call for the end of occupation and the catastrophic military onslaughts and illegal settlement activities in Palestine. However, at no point can the terrorist actions of the Hamas be condoned. They must not be allowed to use the innocent people of Gaza to achieve their own objectives. As we all know, it is the killing of some 1,200 Israelis and the taking of another 250 hostage on 07th October, 2023 by the Hamas which set off this massive Israeli offensive. The sad truth is that it is the innocent on both sides who have paid and are paying with their lives for terrorism on both sides.\n\nTherefore, Sir, it is a moment for Sri Lanka to rise to our moral responsibility, to honour our legacy and to join the growing chorus of nations which choose justice over expediency.\n\nThank you very much. \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0dc3\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd6\u0daa \u0db8\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd3\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0ba4\u0bae\u0bc8\u0bae\u0bae\u0ba4\u0bbe\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b89\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Presiding Member) \u0db8\u0dd3\u0dc5\u0d9f\u0da7 \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d9c\u0d9c\u0db8\u0dd0\u0dad\u0dd2\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dd2\u0dba. \u0d94\u0dd9\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dd2\u0dba\u0da7 \u0dd2\u0dc3\u0db1\u0dcf\u0da9\u0dd2 . \u0dcf\u0dbd\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dca \u0dad\u0dd2\u0dc0\u0dd9\u0db1\u0dd9\u0dcf."
  },
