    "chunk_text": "Sir, let me recall one striking example. The global technology giant Motorola once considered Sri Lanka as a potential destination for its operations. But, due to instability and policy uncertainty, they chose Malaysia instead. That single investment became a spark for Malaysia\u2019s transformation into a technology and manufacturing hub. Not only Motorola, but many other international companies bypassed Sri Lanka and invested in the UAE, Singapore and Malaysia, nations which had political stability, clear policy frameworks and investor confidence. That was a painful but important lesson for us. Opportunities lost cannot always be regained, but they can remind us never to repeat the same mistakes.\n\nSir, Sri Lanka and the UAE established diplomatic relations in 1979. Since then, our bilateral partnership has grown steadily in trade, investment and people-to-people ties. The UAE is home to nearly 300,000 Sri Lankan expatriates. They contribute significantly to the UAE\u2019s economy while also sending their valuable remittances home. These men and women are our unofficial ambassadors, strengthening the bonds of trust and friendship between our two countries. Trade between our nations is equally vital. The UAE is Sri Lanka\u2019s seventh largest export market and the third largest source of import.\n\nAnd also, this is not only about money, but about knowledge sharing, technology transferring and positioning Sri Lanka firmly on the global investment map.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0dc3\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd6\u0daa \u0db8\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd3\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0ba4\u0bae\u0bc8\u0bae\u0bae\u0ba4\u0bbe\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b89\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Presiding Member) \u0daf\u0dd0\u0db1\u0dca \u0dcf\u0dcf\u0dd9 \u0d9c\u0dd9\u0dc3\u0db1\u0dca \u0dba\u0db1\u0dca\u0db1, \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0db1\u0dca\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dad\u0da2\u0dd3\u0dc0\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad \u0db8\u0d9c\u0dba\u0da0\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0daf\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0db8\u0dd6\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dad\u0dd2 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bb1\u0b9c\u0bc0\u0bb5\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0b9a\u0b9c\u0baf\u0b9a\u0bcd\u0bc6\u0ba8\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0bae\u0bc2\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf) (The Hon. Rajeevan Jeyachandramoorthy) Sir, give me a minute."
