    "chunk_text": "Therefore, I am very grateful to the people who have petitioned again to revive the matter. Then, the OMP went there. On the 26th of August, 2025, an expert team including Judicial Medical Officers, forensic anthropologists and archaeologists submitted a request to the Court to go to the mass grave site, as per the Order made. Even now, as we speak, that team is visiting that place; I was told that they were going there and the OMP is handling everything. Based on their findings, they will submit an interim report and then, the Magistrate will give the order for excavation and exhumations.\n\n(ii) Hon. Member, the means and methods of inquiry, as you know, would be decided based on the opinions of the experts including JMOs, forensic anthropologists, archaeologists, the police, crime scene investigators and in accordance with international protocols. My Ministry will fully facilitate the process, using modern and advanced technologies to ensure accuracy, efficiency and the preservation of evidence. These technologies would enable more targeted and minimally invasive excavations, minimizing the risk of damaging potential evidence and ensuring that the process adheres to international best practices and Standard Operating Procedures in forensic archaeology and human rights investigations. The ultimate objective is to ensure a scientifically rigorous and transparent excavation process which upholds judicial inquiry and delivers justice to the families of the victims. So, I assure you that it will be done, that we will use technology, and if we do not have the necessary technology here, we will ask our international friends to provide that to us. Anyway, we will do so.\n\n(iii) The Court will determine the collaboration of"
